  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\n- Dry with Morning Fog\n\nOur period of dry weather will continue through the weekend. A\nshortwave trough and associated front will swing through this\nevening. This is currently located in the UP into northern\nWisconsin. There is limited moisture with this disturbance,\ntherefore only expecting some cloud cover to move in. Skies clear\novernight with a moderate inversion developing and temperatures\nfalling into the upper 30s to low 40s. HREF and REFS show a 40 to\n60 percent chance of visibilities less than a mile across much of\nthe area. The best chances are north of I-94. Fog could bring \nslow downs for the Thursday morning commute.\n\nThrough the rest of the week we'll see mostly sunny skies with \nhighs in the 60s and lows in the upper 30s to mid 40s. There is\nthe potential for fog each morning as well.\n\n- Chances for Rain Return Next Week\n\nThe upper level pattern changes for next week bringing several\nshortwave troughs through the region along with better moisture.\nThis can be seen in the long range ensemble members that start to\nbring in precipitation chances as early as Monday. More members\nare dry Monday, therefore the NBM does not highlight any chances.\nA larger number of members show rain Tuesday into Wednesday with \nchances likely lingering through the rest of the week.",
